.SH "NAME"
pcre2_set_recursion_memory_management \- obsolete function that does nothing
.SH "SYNOPSIS"
.sp
.ss \n[.ss]
.nf
.fam C
\fB\&#include\fP \fB<pcre2.h>\fP

\fBint\fP pcre2_set_recursion_memory_management(
      \fBpcre2_match_context\fP *\fImcontext\fP,
      \fBvoid\fP *(*\fImymalloc\fP)(\fBsize_t\fP \fIsize\fP, \fBvoid\fP *\fImydata\fP),
      \fBvoid\fP (*\fImyfree\fP)(\fBvoid\fP *\fIptr\fP, \fBvoid\fP *\fImydata\fP),
      \fBvoid\fP *\fImydata\fP);
.fam
.fi
.ss \n[.ss] 0
.SH "DESCRIPTION"
.sp
From release 10.30 onwards, this function is obsolete and does nothing. The
result is always zero.
.sp
There is a complete description of the PCRE2 native API in the
\f(CRpcre2api\fP
page and a description of the POSIX API in the
\f(CRpcre2posix\fP
page.